<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  {%- set pageTitle = title + " — " + site.name if title else site.title %}
  {#- An essay describes itself: without this every shared essay link showed
      the site blurb instead of what the piece is about. -#}
  {%- if description %}{% set pageDesc = description %}
  {%- elif layout == 'essay.njk' %}{% set pageDesc = content | excerpt(180) %}
  {%- else %}{% set pageDesc = site.description %}{% endif %}
  {%- set pageUrl = site.url + page.url %}
  <title>{{ pageTitle }}</title>
  <meta name="description" content="{{ pageDesc }}">
  <link rel="canonical" href="{{ pageUrl }}">

  {#- Shared everywhere a link is pasted. Without these, every share renders
      as a bare URL with no title card. -#}
  <meta property="og:type" content="{{ 'article' if layout == 'essay.njk' else 'website' }}">
  <meta property="og:site_name" content="{{ site.name }}">
  <meta property="og:locale" content="{{ site.locale }}">
  <meta property="og:title" content="{{ title if title else site.title }}">
  <meta property="og:description" content="{{ pageDesc }}">
  <meta property="og:url" content="{{ pageUrl }}">
  <meta property="og:image" content="{{ site.url }}/img/og.png">
  <meta property="og:image:width" content="1200">
  <meta property="og:image:height" content="630">
  <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image">
  {%- if layout == 'essay.njk' %}
  <meta property="article:published_time" content="{{ page.date | isoDate }}">
  {%- endif %}

  <link rel="icon" href="/img/icon.png" type="image/png">
  <link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="/img/icon.png">
  <link rel="alternate" type="application/rss+xml" title="{{ site.name }}" href="/feed.xml">

  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
  <link href="/css/style.css" rel="stylesheet">
  {#- The rail art is 428KB. A fresh document must fetch and decode it before
      it can paint the rail, so without this the illustration pops in a frame
      or two after the rest of the page on every navigation. -#}
  <link rel="preload" as="image" href="/img/rail-2.png">
  <link rel="preload" as="image" href="/img/bust.png">
  {#- Blocking, and deliberately in <head>: the persisted width has to be on
      <html> BEFORE first paint. Applied from view-toggle.js at the end of
      <body> it lands a frame late, so every navigation painted split view
      first and then snapped. Key must match KEY in view-toggle.js. -#}
  <script>
    (function () {
      var v = "split";
      try { if (localStorage.getItem("ikinari:view") === "full") v = "full"; } catch (e) {}
      document.documentElement.setAttribute("data-view", v);
      // Gates the seam toggle: without JS it would render as a real button
      // that does nothing. Same reasoning as building copy buttons in JS.
      document.documentElement.classList.add("js");
    })();
  </script>
</head>
<body>
  <div class="split">

    <div class="pane">
      <header class="masthead">
        <span class="sig">Rizky Maulana</span>
        {% include "sound-toggle.njk" %}
        <img src="/img/bust.png" alt="" width="130" height="200">
      </header>

      {#- aria-current is the semantic half of the vermilion rule. Without it
          the active tab is marked by a CSS class alone, which conveys nothing
          to assistive tech — the visual state had no counterpart. -#}
      <nav class="tabs" aria-label="Sections">
        <a class="tab{% if section == 'essays' %} is-active{% endif %}" href="/"
           {% if section == 'essays' %}aria-current="page"{% endif %}>
          <i></i><span>Essays</span>
        </a>
        <a class="tab{% if section == 'experience' %} is-active{% endif %}" href="/experience/"
           {% if section == 'experience' %}aria-current="page"{% endif %}>
          <i></i><span>Experience</span>
        </a>
        <a class="tab{% if section == 'about' %} is-active{% endif %}" href="/about/"
           {% if section == 'about' %}aria-current="page"{% endif %}>
          <i></i><span>About</span>
        </a>
      </nav>

      {#- The router swaps this element and nothing else. The rail, the seam
          and the masthead are never touched, so they cannot flicker. -#}
      <main class="pane-content">
        {{ content | safe }}
      </main>
    </div>

    {#- A drawer pull clipped to the rail's edge. The chevron always points
        the way the rail is about to move. -#}
    <button class="seam" type="button" title="Toggle reading width  (\)"
            aria-label="Toggle reading width" aria-pressed="false">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2"
           stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
        <path d="M9 6l6 6-6 6"/>
      </svg>
    </button>

    {#- Fixed to the viewport, NOT inside the rail: .rail-inner keeps its width
        and slides out of frame when the rail collapses, so anything in it goes
        off-screen with her. A global preference has to outlive both states. -#}
    {% include "sound-toggle.njk" %}

    <aside class="rail">
      {#- The inner keeps its own width while the column closes, so she slides
          out of frame at full proportions instead of being squashed. -#}
      <div class="rail-inner">
        <img src="/img/rail-2.png" alt="Commissioned illustration of Fujimasa March">

        {#- A signature block, not a nav bar: the details, then the name. The
            heaviest element anchors the bottom edge. Links from site.json so
            there is one place to change them. -#}
        <div class="rail-foot">
          <div class="rail-links">
            <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">EMAIL</a>
            <a href="{{ site.github }}" rel="me">GITHUB</a>
            <a href="{{ site.linkedin }}" rel="me">LINKEDIN</a>
          </div>
          <span class="sig">Rizky Maulana</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </aside>

  </div>

  <script src="/js/sound.js"></script>
  <script src="/js/router.js"></script>
  <script src="/js/view-toggle.js"></script>
  <script src="/js/code-copy.js"></script>

</body>
</html>
